From 16cc926548b2740d031733a1e92325112ca10fba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kuzma30 <kuzemkoa@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:28:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] Modeling Algorithms - Fillet a concave edge first where
 it meets two convex fillets

FreeCAD issue 20085 (cube 20 with fillets of radius 6 and a square hole 8 x 8
whose walls run along the tangent lines of the fillets): a vertical (concave)
edge of the hole and the two upper (convex) edges at its end, filleted
together (Edge26 + Edge13 + Edge35), met at a vertex which also has smooth
edges (between the fillets and the sphere of the cube). The corner of the three
fillets was a plate patch with tolerance 0.0068 (r = 0.5) to 0.21 (r = 2.5).
Filleting the vertical edge first and the upper edges then gives a corner
without patch: the upper fillets go round the end of the vertical one, with
tolerance 2.4e-4 at most.

BRepFilletAPI_MakeFillet::Build now does so when a concave contour ends at a
vertex where two convex contours end too and the vertex has more edges than
contour ends: the concave contours ending at such vertices are filleted first,
then the other contours on the result, the edges of the input being replaced by
their images in the intermediate shape (the edges of the result shared by the
images of the faces of the edge and lying on it). The fillets of the second
stage propagate round the ends of the first ones, so this is done only if, at
each end of a first-stage contour, the other sharp edges are all filleted or
none; otherwise, or if a stage fails, the contours are computed together as
before. Only contours of constant radius are handled; the parameters given to
SetParams and SetContinuity are passed on to the stages.

The history (Generated, Modified, IsDeleted) of a result computed in two
stages is the merge of the histories of the stages (BRepTools_History): the
edges of the second stage modified from the edges of the input, and the new
edges of the faces of the first stage generated from its contours, so that the
faces of the second stage built on them are related to the input.

The cap closing a fillet in the plane of a section or in the tangent plane at
its end (CapInSectionPlane) is recorded as generated from the vertex, like the
other corners.

Tests: the DRAW test fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_three_fillets_corner
(r = 0.5 to 2.5, compared with the fillets made in two steps) and the GTest
SquareHoleInRoundedCube_ThreeFilletsCornerAsInTwoSteps (also checking that
every face of the result is related to the input by the history). The
expected results of fillet_rounded_cube_all_edges_symmetric (all edges: the
four corners of the hole), fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_concave_edge,
fillet_rounded_cube_square_hole_rim_after_corner and of the corresponding
GTests are updated: the tolerances go down to about 1e-4 and the volumes are
those of the fillets made in two steps.

